            <ArticleTitle>PulseCath, a new short-term ventricular assist device: our experience in off-pump coronary artery bypass graft surgery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>423-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2459/JCM.0b013e3282eee851</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We utilized a new ventricular assist device, the PulseCath catheter, to perform an off-pump bypass procedure in a patient with low ejection fraction. The 21 Fr PulseCath catheter, driven by a standard intra-aortic balloon pump console, can generate a pulsatile flow of 2-3 l/min. The PulseCath coupled with an intra-aortic balloon pump device is an important tool for left ventricular assistance.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
